  "query_preview": ".. High pressure looks to be the main driver of the\nsynoptic pattern through at least the middle of next week, with no \norganized systems on the horizon. This weekend will temperatures \nwill rebound back towards normal as return southwesterly flow sets \nup over the region. Temperatures will continue to trend a few \ndegrees warmer each day next week with highs by the middle of the \nweek forecast to top 70 degrees across much of the region. With \nreturn to seasonally above normal temperatures and a prolonged dry \nperiod into next week will need to monitor fuels across drought \nstricken areas of northern WI to the possibility of an increased \nwildfire risk.",
